{{Quote|We're going to Jedha. That's a war zone.|Jyn Erso to Cassian Andor prior to their mission|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
Some time before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the '''Jedha insurgency''' was carried out by [[Saw Gerrera]]'s [[Partisans]] on the [[desert]] [[moon]] of [[Jedha]] as part of their [[Campaigns of Saw Gerrera's Partisans|larger campaign]] against the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> Gerrera had long been investigating the Empire's [[Project Stardust|secret weapons project]] and learned of the Empire's interest in the [[Jedha system]] from the [[technician]] [[Mich Matt]] during his [[mission to Faos Station]].<ref name="Name">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref>

Under the rule of the Empire, which enforced an '''occupation of Jedha''' to protect its [[kyber crystal]] [[mining]] operation, the ancient streets of [[Jedha City]] were heavily occupied in particular.<ref name="Rogue One Visual Guide" /> The city found its occupation increased due to Gerrera's operations. [[Stormtrooper]]s, [[TX-225 GAVw "Occupier" combat assault tank]]s, and [[All Terrain Scout Transport]]s did battle with the Partisans amongst the streets.<ref name="Rogue One" /> In spite of the Imperial occupation and Partisan counteroffensive, Jedha City was still visited by many offworlders.<ref name="Rogue One Visual Guide" /> At one point, Rebel [[soldier]]s [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] and [[Sergeant]] [[Jyn Erso]] undertook a [[Battle on Jedha|mission to Jedha]] to secure [[Bodhi Rook]] and locate Gerrera.<ref name="Rogue One" />

